    "name": "monokai",
    "note": "Monokai Pro (VS Code: 'Monokai Pro Light' / 'Monokai Pro', monokai.theme-monokai-pro-vscode 2.0.16). Surfaces, text and the six hues are the VS Code themes' own; the terminal is their integrated terminal's palette, where blue IS the orange (Monokai Pro has no blue). The accent is the cyan in both modes: the source's UI accent is yellow in dark (the shell's spill/drain colour) and the error pink in light, either of which would make a state unreadable. Teal, blue and pink are not in the palette: mixes of its neighbours. The terminal's bright blue (color12), which the source fills with the orange once more, is a blue: the bar's Bluetooth and LLM glyphs need one apart from the cyan and the purple. Group tabs: the tab is the orange (warn), a locked group's tab the purple. btop: custom (btop's own monokai is the classic Monokai on #060604, not the Pro; the files are monokai-light and monokai-dark, apart from btop's monokai.theme). The pair was monokai-pro until 2026-11-08 (themectl install renames it in your home).",
